Package: sslcrtsrv-client
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-cryptography
Recommends: python3-rich
Description: SSLCrtSrv client - request and retrieve managed certificates
 Client tool (scs-client) for the SSLCrtSrv certificate management
 system: registers a host with an SSLCrtSrv server, requests certificates for
 given FQDNs, and retrieves issued key/certificate/intermediate files.
 .
 python3-rich is optional: scs-client listcerts/info fall back to plain
 text output without it, rather than requiring it.
 .
 Install sslcrtsrv-server instead on the host running the certificate server
 itself.

Package: sslcrtsrv-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         adduser,
         sslcrtsrv-client (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3-sqlalchemy,
         python3-alembic,
         python3-textual,
         python3-pytz,
         python3-rich
Recommends: acme.sh,
            bind9-dnsutils
Suggests: python3-pymysql,
          python3-psycopg2,
          python3-josepy,
          python3-maxminddb
Description: SSLCrtSrv server - certificate management server and admin tools
 Server-side tools for the SSLCrtSrv certificate management system:
 .
  * scs-server - the TCP server clients register/request against
  * scs-crtmanager / scs-cltmanager - certificate and client
    administration CLIs
  * scs-crtrequest - requests/renews certificates via acme.sh
  * scs-admintui - full-screen terminal admin dashboard
  * scs-dbmigrate - one-time schema upgrades and cross-backend data
    migration for the database (SQLite by default; MySQL/MariaDB and
    PostgreSQL are also supported, see Manual.MD)
  * scs-acme-server - optional RFC 8555 ACME protocol server, letting
    other ACME clients request certificates through this server instead
    of (or alongside) the native scs-client protocol
 .
 acme.sh itself is not packaged for Debian and must be installed separately
 (see https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh) if you intend to use
 scs-crtrequest. bind9-dnsutils (for `dig`) is needed for scs-crtrequest's
 DNS delegation check, which runs by default (pass --no-check-dns to skip
 it instead).
 .
 python3-pymysql/python3-psycopg2 are only needed if you configure the
 MySQL/MariaDB or PostgreSQL database backend respectively - the default
 SQLite backend needs neither. python3-josepy is only needed if you run
 scs-acme-server; nothing else in this package imports it. python3-maxminddb
 is only needed if you configure geoip_database_path with the default
 "maxmind" geoip_backend, for GeoIP country-based access control; the
 alternative "ip2location" backend has no Debian package and needs
 `pip install IP2Location` into a venv instead.
